From: xtandard-image
Subject: [PATCH] The planar alpha plane must match the image

Found by fuzzing (Go FuzzJXR, confirmed with ASan): the planar alpha
plane's own codestream header could turn its output into 32-bit floats
(or another size) while it is written into the image's 8-bit pixels,
past the end of the caller's buffer. Fail the decode when the alpha plane's
sample type or size differs from the image's.
---
--- a/jxrgluelib/JXRGlueJxr.c
+++ b/jxrgluelib/JXRGlueJxr.c
@@ -2148,6 +2148,11 @@
         if (0 == pID->WMP.DecoderCurrAlphaMBRow) // add this to WMP struct!
         {
             FailIf(ICERR_OK != ImageStrDecInit(&pID->WMP.wmiI_Alpha, &pID->WMP.wmiSCP_Alpha, &pID->WMP.ctxSC_Alpha), WMP_errFail);
+            // The alpha plane is written into the image's pixels: its
+            // codestream must not change the sample type or the size.
+            FailIf(pID->WMP.wmiI_Alpha.bdBitDepth != pID->WMP.wmiI.bdBitDepth ||
+                pID->WMP.wmiI_Alpha.cWidth != pID->WMP.wmiI.cWidth ||
+                pID->WMP.wmiI_Alpha.cHeight != pID->WMP.wmiI.cHeight, WMP_errFail);
         }
         
         // Re-entrant mode incurs 1 MBR delay, so to get 0th MBR, we have to ask for 1st MBR
